{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Policy Gradient \u2014 REINFORCE from Scratch Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: softmax policy network"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def policy_logits(theta, state_features):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [dot(theta[a], state_features) for a in range(N_ACTIONS)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def softmax(logits):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    m = max(logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    exps = [exp(l - m) for l in logits]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    Z = sum(exps)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [e / Z for e in exps]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Use a linear policy (one weight vector per action) for a tabular env. For Atari, swap in a CNN and keep the softmax head."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: sampling and log-probability"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def sample_action(probs, rng):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    x = rng.random()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cum = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for a, p in enumerate(probs):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        cum += p"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if x <= cum:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            return a"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return len(probs) - 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def log_prob(probs, a):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return log(probs[a] + 1e-12)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: rollout with log-probs captured"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def rollout(theta, env, rng, gamma):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    trajectory = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    s = env.reset()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    while not done:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        logits = policy_logits(theta, s)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        probs = softmax(logits)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        a = sample_action(probs, rng)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        s_next, r, done = env.step(s, a)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        trajectory.append((s, a, r, probs))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        s = s_next"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return trajectory"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: REINFORCE update"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def reinforce_step(theta, trajectory, gamma, lr, baseline=0.0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    returns = compute_returns(trajectory, gamma)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for (s, a, _, probs), G in zip(trajectory, returns):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        advantage = G - baseline"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        grad_log_pi_a = [-p for p in probs]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        grad_log_pi_a[a] += 1.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(N_ACTIONS):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for j in range(len(s)):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                theta[i][j] += lr * advantage * grad_log_pi_a[i] * s[j]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The gradient `\u2207 log \u03c0(a|s) = e_a - \u03c0(\u00b7|s)` (onehot of `a` minus probabilities) is the heart of softmax policy gradients. Burn it into muscle memory."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: baselines"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "A running mean of `G` over recent episodes is enough variance reduction to get a 4\u00d74 GridWorld running; it takes ~500 episodes to converge. Upgrade the baseline to a learned `V\u0302(s)` and you get actor-critic."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Implement REINFORCE on 4\u00d74 GridWorld with a linear softmax policy. Train for 1,000 episodes without a baseline. Plot the learning curve; measure variance (std of returns).\n2. **Medium.** Add a running-mean baseline. Train again. Compare sample efficiency and variance to the vanilla run. By how much does the baseline reduce steps to convergence?\n3. **Hard.** Add an entropy bonus `\u03b2 \u00b7 H(\u03c0)`. Sweep `\u03b2 \u2208 {0, 0.01, 0.1, 1.0}`. Plot final return and policy entropy. Where is the sweet spot on this task?"
      ]
    }
